AIM

To demonstrate various string operations in Python such as finding the length, changing case, accessing characters, slicing, searching, replacing, checking membership, concatenation, and trimming spaces.

ALGORITHM

Start the program.
Create a string s with the value " Hello Python".
Display the original string.
Find and display the length of the string using len().
Convert and display the string in uppercase using upper().
Convert and display the string in lowercase using lower().
Display the character at index 6.
Find and display the position of "Python" using find().
Extract and display a portion of the string using slicing.
Replace "Python" with "Universe" using replace().
Check whether "Python" is present in the string using the in operator.
Concatenate the string with " programming".
Create another string "Hello World".
Remove leading and trailing spaces using strip().
Display all results.
Stop the program.

SOURCE CODE

s = " Hello Python"

print("Original String:", s)
print("Length:", len(s))
print("Uppercase:", s.upper())
print("Lowercase:", s.lower())
print("Character at index 6:", s[6])
print("Position of Python:", s.find("Python"))
print("Slice:", s[1:7])
print("Replace:", s.replace("Python", "Universe"))
print("After Replace:", s)
print("Contains Python:", "Python" in s)
print("Concatenation:", s + " programming")

s2 = "Hello World"
print("Trim:", s2.strip())

